  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The predictive model relies on video data collected from a relatively small sample of 10 specific locations within a single country.",
      "what": "The study analyzed 40 hours of aerial video footage across 10 shared-use paths in the Czech Republic using the YOLO and BoT-SORT algorithms to track user trajectories, speeds, and interactions. Machine learning models were trained on 15-minute interval data to predict traffic conflicts based on path width, user volumes, and transport modes.",
      "why": "It establishes a quantitative link between physical path design and user safety, demonstrating that wider paths directly mitigate conflict risks while congestion—characterized by high volumes, low speeds, and a high share of cyclists—increases them."
